@startuml Transfer_Flow_Async_Tier3
!theme plain
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Figure 4.7 — Async Tier 3 ML Analysis (Post-Hoc, Non-Blocking)

participant "Fraud Service\n:8086\n(fraudAsyncExecutor)" as FRAUD
participant "Fraud DB\n(fraud schema)" as DB

note over FRAUD
  Triggered by Tier2AsyncRunner.runTier3Only()
  only when synchronous Tier 1 + Tier 2 returned ALLOW.
  Runs in a dedicated thread pool — does NOT block
  the transfer response already sent to the user.
end note

== Tier 3 ML Inference ==
FRAUD -> FRAUD : Load FraudEvaluationRequest\nfrom in-memory context
FRAUD -> FRAUD : Build feature vector (6 dimensions):\n[0] amountRatio = amount / 50,000\n[1] typeRisk = {INTERNAL:1.0, EXTERNAL:3.0}\n[2] hourSuspicion = {01-05h:3.0, night:2.0, day:1.0}\n[3] newAccountFlag = 1.0 if age < 30d\n[4] senderDepletionRatio = amount / oldBalance\n[5] isRoundAmount = 1.0 if amount % 100 ≈ 0
FRAUD -> FRAUD : Apply MinMax scaling\n(per-feature min/max saved at training time)
FRAUD -> FRAUD : IsolationForest.score(scaledFeatures)\n→ anomalyScore ∈ [0, 1]

== Decision ==
alt anomalyScore > calibrated threshold (≈ 0.55–0.75)
  == Post-Hoc FLAG ==
  FRAUD -> FRAUD : PerturbationAnalyzer:\ncompute feature importances\n(replace each feature with training mean,\nmeasure |score change|)
  FRAUD -> FRAUD : ReasoningBuilder:\nbuild human-readable explanation\n(primary + secondary anomaly drivers)
  FRAUD -> DB : UPDATE fraud_decision SET\n  status = FLAG,\n  decided_by_tier = TIER3_ML,\n  risk_score = anomalyScore * 100,\n  explanation = "Tier3-ML post-hoc FLAG: ..."
  note right of DB
    Admin dashboard will surface
    this as an unresolved alert.
    Transfer is already completed —
    this is a post-hoc learning signal.
  end note
else anomalyScore ≤ threshold
  FRAUD -> DB : No update — existing ALLOW decision stands
end

@enduml
